From 79477b7501f4271ba540f06b518689a8cab03596 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 06:24:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent): a gateway-hosted Desktop turn waits for a held
 turn lease instead of refusing it [daveey]

A send to a busy Desktop chat that reached the owner gateway (forwarded by the serve backend, or a
cross_session relay) failed at once with session_busy, "Couldn't send your message", and the text was
lost. The gateway's agent for a Desktop (gui) local chat carries the session surface as its platform
("desktop"), so admit_durable_turn_lease gave it the Desktop serve rule wait_seconds=0, which exists
because a serve client still holds the text and offers Take over. A gateway FIFO turn has already
accepted the input, so nobody holds it any more. refuses_held_lease_at_once() keeps the instant refusal
only for Desktop/TUI turns with no gateway_session_key. A gateway-hosted turn waits up to
LEASE_WAIT_SECONDS like every other gateway turn ("waiting for it to finish" status; /stop aborts) and
runs once the holder releases.

Five whys (MacBook, session 20261026_235722_bef6c6, 2026-11-02 21:44:58 / 21:45:29 PST)
Problem: two Desktop sends of "turn it back on" came back "Couldn't send your message / Your request
  was not processed" (failure_reason=session_busy) and were lost until an agent relayed the text at
  22:01. A cross_session relay at 21:53 was refused the same way.
Why 1: the turn that ran the send failed lease admission at once: agent.log "session turn lease wait
  timed out", lease held by another desktop-platform turn, wait_seconds=0. Code:
  agent/turn_facade_lease.py:534 (wait 0 for platform in {desktop, tui}).
Why 2: that turn was a gateway turn ("gateway.run: inbound message: platform=local" on pid 46350, port
  9119), not the Desktop serve backend's own turn queue. A serve backend refuses a legacy turn while
  the gateway's durable ledger holds non-terminal work for the chat
  (tui_gateway/session_lifecycle.py _canonical_ledger_refusal) and forwards the typed prompt to the
  ready gateway serving the profile home (tui_gateway/methods_prompt.py _submit_to_ledger_owner,
  tui_gateway/owner_forward.py, RT-37). Desktop's 400 "Chat is not owned by this runtime" on
  /api/plugins/account-usage/selection at the same seconds shows it was not on the owning runtime.
Why 3: the ledger held work: an auto kanban_notice / process_complete admission (evidence for the
  21:53 relay; for 21:44 it is a hypothesis: the logs show the forward, not the admission row).
Why 4: the gateway FIFO and the turn lease are separate fences. The lease holder was a turn outside
  this route's FIFO slot, so the FIFO started the forwarded prompt at once and only the lease saw the
  conflict (hypothesis on which turn: the card names the 2860 s turn ui_session=45b74d93).
Why 5: the gateway's agent for a gui local chat is built with platform=policy.platform="desktop"
  (gateway/session_policy.py SURFACES['gui'], gateway/run_turn_runner.py:1280), and the zero-wait rule
  keyed on that surface label, not on who holds the input.
Root (happened): the zero holder-wait rule was keyed on the session's surface, not on whether the
  turn's input is still in a client composer. A gateway FIFO turn had durably accepted the message and
  refused it anyway, so accepted input was dropped.
Root (not caught): tests/tui_gateway/test_legacy_submit_forwards_to_owner.py drives the owner FIFO with
  _schedule disabled, so the forwarded prompt's turn never ran through the lease. The lease tests cover
  a Desktop serve turn (wait 0) and gateway messaging turns (wait) separately, never a gateway-hosted
  desktop-surface turn against a held lease.
Recurrence: RT-37 (#140385) promised that the owner runs a forwarded prompt "after the current turn,
  exactly once". That held for the owner's own FIFO but not for a lease held outside it, because the
  owner's agent kept the Desktop serve rule.
Countermeasures:
- root: refuses_held_lease_at_once(): an instant refusal only for Desktop/TUI turns without a
  gateway_session_key; gateway-hosted turns wait. The timeout wording follows the same predicate.
  Proof: tests/gateway/test_busy_chat_send_queues_behind_turn.py fails before the change with the live
  text ("This chat has another active writer ... not processed") and passes after.
- detection: that file runs the real gateway agent build (TurnRunner._build_fresh_agent, platform key
  "desktop") and AIAgent.run_conversation against a real SessionDB lease, for both entry paths: the
  Desktop send behind a running turn and the cross_session send behind an automation turn. Each is
  still waiting while the holder runs, then runs exactly once after it releases. Controls: an idle chat
  runs at once; a Desktop serve turn (no gateway key) still refuses a held lease at once (Take over).
- limit: a holder that outlives LEASE_WAIT_SECONDS (1800 s) still ends the wait with the resend notice.
---
 agent/turn_facade_lease.py                    |  18 ++-
 .../test_busy_chat_send_queues_behind_turn.py | 148 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 164 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/gateway/test_busy_chat_send_queues_behind_turn.py

diff --git a/agent/turn_facade_lease.py b/agent/turn_facade_lease.py
index 2abdd551dfc..e87c2760ef7 100644
--- a/agent/turn_facade_lease.py
+++ b/agent/turn_facade_lease.py
@@ -469,6 +469,20 @@ def session_was_taken_over(agent, session_id: str) -> bool:
     return db._session_turn_lease_key(taken) == db._session_turn_lease_key(session_id)
 
 
+def refuses_held_lease_at_once(agent, platform) -> bool:
+    """True for a Desktop/TUI turn its own client submitted: a lease another writer holds is refused
+    at once, because that client still has the text and offers Take over.
+
+    A gateway-hosted turn (``gateway_session_key`` set by the gateway's agent build) differs even when
+    its session's surface is ``desktop``/``tui`` (``session_policy.SURFACES``): the gateway's FIFO
+    already accepted the input (a typed send forwarded to the owner, a cross-session relay), so no
+    composer holds it any more. It waits for the holder like every other gateway turn, which queues
+    the message behind the running turn instead of failing it ``session_busy`` and dropping it."""
+    if platform not in {"desktop", "tui"}:
+        return False
+    return not getattr(agent, "_gateway_session_key", None)
+
+
 def admit_durable_turn_lease(
     agent, *, session_id: str, relay_turn_id: str, task_context: dict[str, Any],
     conversation_history: Optional[list[dict[str, Any]]],
@@ -531,7 +545,7 @@ def admit_durable_turn_lease(
     authority_floor = time.time()  # every acquisition attempt stamps its expiry after this instant
     if not db.acquire_session_turn_lease(
         session_id, holder, ttl_seconds=LEASE_TTL_SECONDS,
-        wait_seconds=0.0 if task_context['platform'] in {"desktop", "tui"} else LEASE_WAIT_SECONDS,
+        wait_seconds=0.0 if refuses_held_lease_at_once(agent, task_context['platform']) else LEASE_WAIT_SECONDS,
         on_wait=_on_wait, on_contended=_on_contended,
         should_abort=lambda: getattr(agent, "_interrupt_requested", False),
         # A busy state.db is not another writer: Desktop/TUI skip the holder wait but must not
@@ -671,7 +685,7 @@ def _lease_not_acquired_result(agent, session_id: str, conversation_history, *,
         "⏳ Another Hermes process kept this session busy too long. Your message was not "
         "processed - wait for the other process to finish, then send it again."
     )
-    if getattr(agent, "platform", None) in {"desktop", "tui"}:
+    if refuses_held_lease_at_once(agent, getattr(agent, "platform", None)):
         timeout_msg = (
             "This chat has another active writer. Use session.take_over (Take over here), "
             "then retry your message. Your message was not processed."
diff --git a/tests/gateway/test_busy_chat_send_queues_behind_turn.py b/tests/gateway/test_busy_chat_send_queues_behind_turn.py
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..21db0f68288
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/gateway/test_busy_chat_send_queues_behind_turn.py
@@ -0,0 +1,148 @@
+"""A send to a busy Desktop chat that reaches the gateway is queued behind the running turn, not refused.
+
+Live (MacBook, 2026-11-02 21:44 PST): Desktop's "turn it back on", typed while another writer's turn held
+the chat, was forwarded to the owner gateway's FIFO and ran there as ``gateway.run: inbound message:
+platform=local``. That gateway turn's agent has the session's surface as its platform (``desktop``,
+``session_policy.SURFACES['gui']``), so ``admit_durable_turn_lease`` gave it the Desktop serve rule,
+``wait_seconds=0``: it failed ``session_busy`` at once and the message was lost ("Couldn't send your
+message"). A cross_session relay at 21:53 died the same way behind an auto kanban_notice turn.
+
+Real: the gateway's agent build (``TurnRunner._build_fresh_agent`` with the ``desktop`` platform key a
+GUI local session carries), ``AIAgent.run_conversation`` with its durable turn lease, the SessionDB lease
+table and the transcript. Replaced: only the provider wire (``native_transport``: answers "ok").
+"""
+import os
+import threading
+import time
+from types import SimpleNamespace
+from unittest.mock import patch
+
+from hermes_state import SessionDB
+from hermes_state_pidns import holder_namespace_token
+from gateway.run_turn_runner import TurnRunner
+from gateway.turn_context import TurnContext
+from gateway.session import Platform, SessionSource
+from run_agent import AIAgent
+from tests.agent import test_model_routing_agent
+from tests.gateway.test_pre_agent_fallback_notice import _runner_with_real_runtime_resolution
+from tests.tui_gateway import test_class_routing
+
+routing_home = test_model_routing_agent.routing_home
+streaming_route = test_model_routing_agent.streaming_route
+native_transport = test_class_routing.native_transport
+
+SID = "20261026_235722_bef6c6"
+
+
+def _running_turn(db, turn):
+    """Another writer's live turn on the chat (this process's pid, so it is never reaped as dead)."""
+    holder = f"pid={os.getpid()}{holder_namespace_token()}:turn={turn}:platform=desktop"
+    assert db.try_acquire_session_turn_lease(SID, holder, ttl_seconds=300)
+    return holder
+
+
+def _gateway_turn(db, routing_home):
+    """The gateway's own agent for a Desktop (gui) local chat, built the way the FIFO turn builds it."""
+    runner = _runner_with_real_runtime_resolution()
+    runner._session_db = db
+    ctx = TurnContext(
+        source=SessionSource(platform=Platform.LOCAL, chat_id="local-chat", user_id="desktop"),
+        message="", history=[], session_id=SID, session_key="agent:main:local:dm:local-chat",
+        user_config=routing_home, AIAgent=AIAgent,
+        resolve_display_setting=lambda *_a: False, _run_still_current=lambda: True,
+        _hooks_ref=SimpleNamespace(loaded_hooks=False),
+    )
+    with patch("gateway.run._resolve_gateway_model", return_value="class:deep"), \
+            patch("gateway.run._get_channel_override", return_value=None):
+        model, runtime = runner._resolve_session_agent_runtime(source=ctx.source, user_config=routing_home)
+    agent = TurnRunner(runner, ctx)._build_fresh_agent(
+        {"model": model, "runtime": runtime}, "desktop", "", 5, None, {}, True)
+    assert agent.platform == "desktop"
+    return agent
+
+
+def _send(agent, text):
+    """Run the turn on a thread (the gateway runs it in an executor); returns (thread, outcome)."""
+    outcome = {}
+
+    def run():
+        outcome["result"] = agent.run_conversation(text)
+        outcome["at"] = time.monotonic()
+
+    thread = threading.Thread(target=run, daemon=True)
+    thread.start()
+    return thread, outcome
+
+
+def _user_rows(db):
+    return [m["content"] for m in db.get_messages(SID) if m["role"] == "user"]
+
+
+def _assert_queued_then_processed(db, agent, holder, text):
+    with patch("model_tools.get_tool_definitions", return_value=[]):
+        thread, outcome = _send(agent, text)
+        time.sleep(2.5)  # a refusing admission returns at once; a queued one is still waiting
+        assert thread.is_alive(), f"refused while the turn ran: {outcome.get('result', {}).get('final_response')}"
+        assert db.session_turn_lease_owner(SID)["holder"] == holder, "the running turn kept the chat"
+        assert text not in _user_rows(db), "nothing of the queued send ran beside the running turn"
+        ended = time.monotonic()
+        db.release_session_turn_lease(SID, holder)  # the running turn ends
+        thread.join(30)
+    assert not thread.is_alive()
+    result = outcome["result"]
+    assert not result.get("failed"), result.get("final_response")
+    assert result.get("failure_reason") != "session_busy"
+    assert result["final_response"] == "ok"
+    assert outcome["at"] >= ended, "it ran after the turn ended"
+    assert _user_rows(db).count(text) == 1, "processed exactly once, in the stored transcript"
+    assert db.session_turn_lease_owner(SID) is None
+    agent.release_clients()
+
+
+def test_desktop_send_while_a_turn_runs_is_processed_after_it(routing_home, native_transport, tmp_path):
+    db = SessionDB(tmp_path / "state.db")
+    db.create_session(SID, source="desktop")
+    holder = _running_turn(db, "45b74d93")
+    _assert_queued_then_processed(db, _gateway_turn(db, routing_home), holder, "turn it back on")
+
+
+def test_cross_session_send_while_an_automation_turn_runs_is_processed_after_it(
+        routing_home, native_transport, tmp_path):
+    db = SessionDB(tmp_path / "state.db")
+    db.create_session(SID, source="desktop")
+    holder = _running_turn(db, "kanban_notice")  # the auto process_complete / kanban_notice turn
+    relay = "[cross_session from @session:default@macbook/20261102_215300_aaaaaa] turn it back on"
+    _assert_queued_then_processed(db, _gateway_turn(db, routing_home), holder, relay)
+
+
+def test_control_idle_chat_runs_at_once(routing_home, native_transport, tmp_path):
+    db = SessionDB(tmp_path / "state.db")
+    db.create_session(SID, source="desktop")
+    agent = _gateway_turn(db, routing_home)
+    started = time.monotonic()
+    with patch("model_tools.get_tool_definitions", return_value=[]):
+        result = agent.run_conversation("turn it back on")
+    assert result["final_response"] == "ok" and not result.get("failed")
+    assert time.monotonic() - started < 2.0, "an idle chat never waits on the lease poll"
+    assert _user_rows(db) == ["turn it back on"]
+    agent.release_clients()
+
+
+def test_control_serve_desktop_turn_still_refuses_a_held_lease_at_once(tmp_path):
+    """A Desktop serve turn its own client submitted (no gateway key) keeps the instant refusal: that
+    client still holds the text and offers Take over."""
+    from agent.turn_facade_lease import admit_durable_turn_lease
+    db = SessionDB(tmp_path / "state.db")
+    db.create_session(SID, source="desktop")
+    _running_turn(db, "other-window")
+    agent = SimpleNamespace(_session_db=db, session_id=SID, platform="desktop", _persist_disabled=False,
+                            _interrupt_requested=False, statuses=[])
+    agent._emit_status = agent._emit_warning = agent.statuses.append
+    started = time.monotonic()
+    admission = admit_durable_turn_lease(
+        agent, session_id=SID, relay_turn_id=f"{SID}:t:x",
+        task_context={"session_id": SID, "task_id": "t", "platform": "desktop"}, conversation_history=[])
+    assert admission.lease is None and admission.early_result is not None
+    assert admission.early_result["failure_reason"] == "session_busy"
+    assert "Take over here" in admission.early_result["final_response"]
+    assert time.monotonic() - started < 2.0
